  "facts": [
    "The Sveti Ilija Tunnel, 4,248 meters long, slices through Biokovo mountain, boasting the highest overburden in Europe at 1,336.5 meters, a record unmatched by any other tunnel on the continent.",
    "Construction began March 25, 2008 from the north, with Hidroelektra niskogradnja drilling northward and Konstruktor from Split advancing from the south, finally meeting on January 21, 2010.",
    "Opened July 8, 2013, the tunnel links the coastal town of Baška Voda to the hinterland of Zagvozd, and since 2018 it has been toll‑free for all drivers."
